================================================================================
  THE DEEP INSIGHT:
    Programs decompose into STRUCTURE (score sequence = indentation/control)
    and CONTENT (arc labels = variable names/expressions).
    This decomposition is THE SAME as tournament score + orientation.
    Compressing them separately always wins (indent-split beats raw zlib).
    This is because structure has LOW entropy (few indentation patterns)
    while content has HIGH entropy (many possible identifiers).
    Tournament theory predicts this: score sequences are constrained
    (Erdos-Gallai conditions), while arc orientations are free.
